# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Burmy — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT environment template.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Never put a real secret in this file — it is committed.
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` is gitignored and must stay so.
#
# Production (Netlify + Supabase) does not use this file at all — production
# environment variables live in Netlify's own dashboard, scoped and secret-
# marked per docs/DEPLOYMENT.md, "Netlify environment-variable policy." This
# template covers local dev only.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development, matching compose.dev.yml.
# In production the host is the internal `dbnet` service name, never localhost.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://burmy:burmy@localhost:5432/burmy

# ── Application ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NODE_ENV=development

# The ONE allowlisted identity. Checked against the verified Cloudflare Access
# JWT claim and again at session creation. There is no signup route.
OWNER_EMAIL=you@example.com

# ── Authentication ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Access with Google is the SOLE authentication mechanism. There is
# no in-app credential, no session cookie of Burmy's own, and no second factor
# — see docs/SECURITY.md, "Authentication".
#
# Verified against Cloudflare's JWKS in src/proxy.ts AND again inside
# requireOwner(), so a route the proxy matcher misses is still enforced.
#
# FAIL CLOSED: these are REQUIRED unless NODE_ENV is exactly `development`.
# Anything else — production, test, staging, or unset — with these missing makes
# the app refuse every request with 503 rather than serve traffic without the
# outer gate. A missing config is an outage; a skipped check is a breach.
#
# Left blank locally, where verification is bypassed by design (no Cloudflare).
# TEAM_DOMAIN accepts `burmy`, `burmy.cloudflareaccess.com`, or the full URL.
CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
CF_ACCESS_AUD=

# After Access is configured, provision the single owner row once:
#   pnpm db:provision-owner
# requireOwner() only ever RESOLVES this row by the verified email — it never
# creates one, so this step has to happen out of band, before the first sign-in.
